{
    "pageid": 5223,
    "title": "Ancestor Worship",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Ancestor worship is a decision that can be taken by any defensive pagan , Tengri pagan, or reformed pagan that has taken the Ancestor Veneration Doctrine . It requires The Old Gods DLC."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Upon taking the decision the player will be the presented with the option of what area they'd like to ask for assistance in. These are limited to Health, Family/Love, War, Prosperity, and Wisdom."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The player will then be presented with the option of what type of sacrifice to make. The options are sacrificing a body part, sacrificing a random prisoner/non-important courtier, a large feast, or a small sacrifice. When sacrificing a body part with The Reaper's Due active, the result will the first one possible of: One-eyed (arguably a positive trait), One-handed , or One-legged ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Based on the previous choices a related event may fire somewhat shortly after using the weights in the following tables (Note that these are weights and not percentages)."
                },
